content.content:
Your questions have been answered: "Quando il caso d'uso risponde con un esito "non felice" ma previsto (domanda mancante, niente di compatibile, dati viaggiatore mancanti), che codice HTTP usiamo e come il client distingue il tipo di risposta?"="200/201 + campo outcome (Recommended)" selected preview:
POST /v1/intents
201 {"outcome":"intent_created", "intent_id":..., "say":...}
200 {"outcome":"question", "question":..., "say":...}

GET /v1/intents/{id}/proposal  (anche reject)
200 {"outcome":"proposal", "proposal_id":..., "product":{...}}
200 {"outcome":"no_match", "failed_criterion":..., "say":...}

POST /v1/proposals/{id}/accept
201 {"outcome":"order", "order_id":..., "payment_url":...}
200 {"outcome":"missing_traveler_data", "missing":[...], "say":...}

GET /v1/orders/{id}
200 {"outcome":"order_status", ...}. You can now continue with these answers in mind.

